🚀 hashtag#Day4: Deploying Multiple Technologies with Docker on EC2 Amazon Linux! 🔥

Today's deep dive covers Dockerizing popular technologies on Amazon Linux EC2, showing step-by-step execution for Nginx, Java, Node.js, and SQL databases!🛠️ 

💡 Before diving into Dockerfiles, ensure your server is ready with:
✅ Docker installation

yum update -y 
yum install docker -y 
systemctl start docker 
systemctl enable docker 

✅ Git installation (to pull real-time source code) 

yum install git -y 
 

📂 How to Use Your Own Source Code:
Want to try deploying your own application using Docker? Follow these steps: 
🔹 Step 1: Clone any public repository containing your source code.

git clone <repository-url> 
cd <repository-directory> 

🔹 Step 2: Modify the Dockerfile according to your application needs.
🔹 Step 3: Build your custom image 
🔹 Step 4: Run and deploy your container


🚀 Writing 4 Dockerfiles – What’s Included Today? 

📝 Dockerfile for Nginx Deployment:

FROM nginx
MAINTAINER name jyothisai
LABEL The nginx web app
EXPOSE 80
COPY . /usr/share/nginx/html/

📝 Dockerfile for Java Application: 

FROM tomcat: 8.0.20-jre8
EXPOSE 8080
COPY tomcat-users.xml /usr/local/tomcat/conf/
COPY target/*.war /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/myapp.war


📝 Dockerfile for Node.js Deployment:

FROM node: 16
WORKDIR /myapp
COPY package*.json./
RUN npm install
COPY . .
CMD ["node", "index.js"]

📝 Dockerfile for SQL Database Creation:

FROM mysql/mysql-server:5.7
EXPOSE 3306
ENV MYSQL_USER=root
ENV MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=admin@123
